# RESOLVER AGENT — FEW-SHOT EXAMPLES

Each example below shows the FULL response shape — the `reasoning`
field is the "comment + draft" pattern: it names the retriever
results, names the cited policy, and enumerates what the model
deliberately did NOT do.

Every case shows ALL 7 fields of `ResolverResult`:
  intent, action, draft, self_check, reasoning, used_entities, hilt_reason
(hilt_reason is `null` when action is `auto_send` or `escalate`).

For the focused per-state routing reference (when to choose
auto_send / hilt_refund / hilt_other / escalate, with 1-2 examples
each), see `state_examples` in the same directory.

Citations use `<policy_id> §<clause>` — no hyperlinks, no prose.

---

## Case 1 — defective item, customer wants a replacement (hilt_other)

Inbound:
  subject: Defective Razer BlackShark
  body: My Razer BlackShark V2 Pro arrived defective (dead audio on
        one side). I want a replacement, not a refund. Order ID is
        <order_id>.

Retriever context (interpreting tool results):
  customer:  <customer_name> (email verified)
  order:     found=true, status=delivered, items=[<Razer BlackShark V2 Pro>]
  payments:  1 row, status=success, amount=<amount>
  products:  warranty_text="<product warranty terms>"
  policies:
    - return-policy §3.1: "Reporting Window" (14 days)
    - return-policy §2:   "Eligible Reasons for Return" (manufacturing defect)

Reasoning:
  Read from retriever: customer verified; order found with status=delivered;
  products[].warranty_text is non-null; policies has return-policy §3.1
  and §2.
  Tone: defective product → empathy lead with "We deeply regret the
  inconvenience".
  Did NOT: upsell, volunteer product features, promise a specific
  replacement unit, or quote a stock number.
  Decision: hilt_other (state change — replacement, not money movement)
  per the customer's explicit "I want a replacement, not a refund".

Response:
{
  "intent":         "complaint",
  "action":         "hilt_other",
  "draft":          "We deeply regret the inconvenience with your Razer
                    BlackShark V2 Pro, <customer_name>. Per return-policy
                    §3.1, you are within the 14-day reporting window;
                    per return-policy §2, manufacturing defects are
                    eligible for replacement. Our team is reviewing your
                    request for a replacement unit.",
  "self_check":     {"policy_compliant": true,  "entities_correct": true,
                     "state_change_implied": true, "tone": "neutral"},
  "reasoning":      "Read from retriever: customer verified, order
                    delivered, products[].warranty_text non-null, policies
                    has return-policy §3.1 and §2. Tone: problem → empathy
                    lead. Did NOT: upsell, volunteer features, promise
                    specific unit, quote stock number. Decision: hilt_other
                    (replacement, not money movement).",
  "used_entities":  {"order_id": "<order_id>", "txn_id": null,
                     "product_names": ["Razer BlackShark V2 Pro"]},
  "hilt_reason":    {
    "policy_clause":        "return-policy §3.1",
    "reason_short":         "Defective item, replacement within 14-day window",
    "reason_long":          "Customer reports defective audio on Razer
                             BlackShark V2 Pro (within the 14-day reporting
                             window) and requested replacement, not refund.
                             Replacement is eligible per return-policy §2
                             and warranty terms.",
    "recommended_action":   "approve_replacement",
    "action_target":        "ops_queue",
    "urgency":              "medium",
    "human_skill_required": "tier_1_support"
  }
}

