## Case 2 — duplicate-charge refund (hilt_refund)

Inbound:
  subject: Charged twice
  body: I was charged twice for one order. Order ID is <order_id>.
        Please refund the extra charge.

Retriever context:
  customer:  <customer_name>
  order:     found=true
  payments:  2 rows — 1 success <amount>, 1 failed <amount>
  policies:
    - payment-policy §8: "Failed Transactions" (refund on duplicate debit)
    - refund-policy  §3: "Refund Timelines" (3–7 business days)

Reasoning:
  Read from retriever: customer verified; order found; payments has
  2 rows (one success, one failed of the same amount); policies has
  payment-policy §8 and refund-policy §3.
  Tone: duplicate charge → problem → empathy lead.
  Did NOT: guess the specific transaction amount beyond what the
  retriever returned, promise a faster refund than §3 allows, or
  suggest the customer file a chargeback.
  Decision: hilt_refund (money movement), urgency=high per the
  duplicate-charge pattern.

Response:
{
  "intent":         "refund",
  "action":         "hilt_refund",
  "draft":          "We deeply regret the inconvenience with the duplicate
                    charge on your order <order_id>, <customer_name>. We
                    have confirmed two transactions on your account: a
                    successful payment and a failed attempt of the same
                    amount. Per payment-policy §8 (Failed Transactions)
                    and refund-policy §3 (Refund Timelines), we will
                    refund the failed attempt within 3–7 business days.
                    Our team is reviewing your request.",
  "self_check":     {"policy_compliant": true,  "entities_correct": true,
                     "state_change_implied": true, "tone": "neutral"},
  "reasoning":      "Read from retriever: customer verified, order found,
                    payments has 2 rows (1 success, 1 failed), policies
                    has payment-policy §8 and refund-policy §3. Tone:
                    duplicate-charge → problem → empathy lead. Did NOT:
                    guess txn_id beyond retriever, promise faster than §3,
                    suggest chargeback. Decision: hilt_refund, urgency=high.",
  "used_entities":  {"order_id": "<order_id>", "txn_id": "<txn_id>",
                     "product_names": []},
  "hilt_reason":    {
    "policy_clause":        "refund-policy §3",
    "reason_short":         "Duplicate charge refund within 3–7 day timeline",
    "reason_long":          "Customer charged twice for one order; one
                             transaction succeeded, one failed. The failed
                             transaction is the duplicate. Refund per
                             refund-policy §3 timeline.",
    "recommended_action":   "approve_refund_<amount>",
    "action_target":        "refund_execution",
    "urgency":              "high",
    "human_skill_required": "tier_2_support"
  }
}

